---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Relocate Works"
  description="Read the Relocate Works Terms of Service for website use, research content, visa sponsor job information, paid access, external links, limitations and disclaimers."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero page-hero-gradient">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Terms of Service.</h1>
        <p class="lead">These Terms explain the basic rules for using Relocate Works, including our website content, relocation guides, visa sponsor job research, newsletter updates, and future paid paid access product.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container prose">
        <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> June 28, 2026</p>

        <h2>1. Acceptance of these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using Relocate Works, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, you should not use the website, subscribe to the publication, or purchase any product offered by Relocate Works.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What Relocate Works provides</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works provides relocation research, country guides, visa pathway summaries, cost of living notes, salary context, tax basics, relocation company information, job search guides, and sponsor-friendly job research. The purpose is to help international candidates organize information and make better research decisions.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may publish free content, newsletter previews, paid posts, paid access resources, private updates, job lists, and related educational material. Product features may change as the project develops.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Educational information only</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works content is provided for general educational and research purposes. It is not legal advice, immigration advice, financial advice, tax advice, career placement advice, or a guarantee of any result. You are responsible for verifying information before making decisions.
        </p>

        <h2>4. No immigration, visa or employment guarantee</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works does not guarantee that any employer will sponsor a visa, provide relocation assistance, reply to your application, interview you, hire you, or help you obtain work authorization. Job availability, employer policy, visa rules, salary thresholds, and relocation benefits can change at any time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Labels such as Confirmed, Likely, Unknown, Not Suitable, sponsor confidence, relocation score, or similar terms are research notes only. They are not official determinations and should not replace verification with employers, recruiters, government sources, or qualified professionals.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Monthly and founding yearly access</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works may offer <strong>$9/month</strong> monthly access and <strong>$49/year</strong> founding yearly access for early supporters. Paid access means access to the specific Relocate Works paid product or content area described at the time of purchase while your subscription remains active.
        </p>
        <p>
          Founding yearly pricing is a special early-member price and may be discontinued or increased for new subscribers in the future. New products may have separate pricing. Relocate Works may update product scope, format, delivery method, frequency, or included resources as the business evolves.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a paid product is delivered through a third-party platform, access may also depend on that platform’s rules, availability, and technical limitations. Users are responsible for using the same email or account information needed to verify access.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Payments and refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Payment terms will be shown at checkout or on the product page. Because this is an early-stage digital information product, refund rules may depend on the payment platform, product type, and access already delivered. Any refund policy should be reviewed before purchase.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a payment problem occurs, contact Relocate Works with the email used for purchase, payment date, and transaction details. We may require proof of purchase before granting access or support.
        </p>

        <h2>7. User responsibilities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Use Relocate Works content for personal research and lawful purposes only.</li>
          <li>Verify visa, job, salary, tax, and relocation information with official and employer sources.</li>
          <li>Do not share paid content, private links, job archives, or member-only resources without permission.</li>
          <li>Do not scrape, copy, resell, redistribute, or repackage Relocate Works content as your own product.</li>
          <li>Do not misuse the website, attempt unauthorized access, or interfere with site security.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works content, branding, page structure, written guides, summaries, and original materials are protected by intellectual property rights. You may read and use the content for personal research, but you may not copy, reproduce, republish, sell, or redistribute substantial portions without written permission.
        </p>

        <h2>9. External links</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works may link to third-party websites including job boards, employer pages, government websites, relocation companies, payment processors, newsletters, and social platforms. We are not responsible for their content, accuracy, availability, privacy practices, pricing, or actions.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes to content and service</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works is an evolving project. We may add, modify, remove, or reorganize content, pages, product features, pricing, countries covered, job categories, publishing frequency, and delivery methods. We may also pause or discontinue features if they are no longer practical, safe, accurate, or sustainable.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, Relocate Works is not liable for losses related to job applications, visa outcomes, immigration decisions, relocation costs, employment decisions, financial decisions, third-party services, outdated information, unavailable job posts, or reliance on website content. Use the information as a starting point for research, not as final advice.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Termination or access restrictions</h2>
        <p>
          We may restrict access to paid or free resources if a user abuses the service, shares private content without permission, violates these Terms, attempts unauthorized access, or uses the product in a way that harms Relocate Works or other users.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Updates to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms as Relocate Works grows. Continued use of the website or paid product after updates means you accept the revised Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions about these Terms, contact Relocate Works through the contact page or the email address listed on the website.
        </p>

        <p class="legal-note"><strong>Note:</strong> These Terms are a practical early-stage template and are not legal advice. If Relocate Works becomes a larger paid platform, consult a qualified legal professional.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
